---
/**
 * About.astro
 * About section — professional summary, career story, values.
 * Tech-first framing with education as a strength.
 */
---
 
<section class="about section section--muted" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
  <div class="container">
 
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h2 class="section-header__title" id="about-heading">
        Building systems that work for people
      </h2>
      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
 
    <div class="about__grid">
 
      <div class="about__primary">
        <p>
          I’m a software engineer based in the UK, building full-stack applications and structured data systems using JavaScript, React, Node.js, Python and SQL. 
        </p>
        <p>
          My work focuses on accessibility, maintainable architecture, and designing software that remains usable in real-world conditions; particularly where users are managing complexity, time pressure, or cognitive load.
        </p>
        <p>
          My experience prior to software engineering, is in education leadership and digital learning design. That background strengthened my systems thinking, communication skills, and understanding of how information design affects usability and decision-making.
        </p>
        <p>
          After completing an MA in Digital Education, I realised I particularly enjoyed designing digital products and wanted to learn software engineering so I could build systems from scratch, rather than relying on platforms with fixed constraints.
        </p>
        <p>
          As I developed my engineering skills, I found I genuinely enjoyed the creativity, challenge, and satisfaction of building, testing, debugging, and iterating on products, especially when working to make them accessible and usable for the widest range of users possible.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside continuing to work in education, I now build full-stack applications focused on usability, accessibility, and structured problem solving, applying testing, API integration, secure coding practices, and iterative delivery to create reliable, maintainable systems.
        </p>
      </div>
 
      <aside class="about__values" aria-label="Core values">
        <h3 class="about__values-heading">What I care about</h3>
        <ul role="list" class="about__values-list">
          <li class="about__value">
            <span class="about__value-icon" aria-hidden="true">⬡</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Accessibility-first</strong>
              <p>Building accessibility into architecture, interaction, and testing from the beginning.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="about__value">
            <span class="about__value-icon" aria-hidden="true">⬡</span>
            <div>
              <strong>User-centred systems</strong>
              <p>Designing systems that remain usable under time pressure, and real-world constraints.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="about__value">
            <span class="about__value-icon" aria-hidden="true">⬡</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Clear, maintainable code</strong>
              <p>Modular, readable systems designed for long-term maintainability.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="about__value">
            <span class="about__value-icon" aria-hidden="true">⬡</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Inclusion by design</strong>
              <p>Designing with a broad range of users, access needs, and working conditions in mind. Including disabled, neurodivergent, and chronically ill users.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
 
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
 
<style>
  .about__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }
 
  @media (min-width: 56em) {
    .about__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 18rem;
      gap: var(--space-16);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
 
  /* Primary text */
  .about__primary p {
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
 
  /* Values sidebar */
  .about__values {
    background-color: var(--color-white);
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }
 
  .about__values-heading {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
 
  .about__values-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    list-style: none;
  }
 
  .about__value {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
 
  .about__value-icon {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: 1.4;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
 
  .about__value strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
 
  .about__value p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
 
